From 4699f31752958fe31887707031a6f2e9ef6d63db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:17:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve bounded tokenizer copy and explicit NUL termination

Keep the measured removal of printf formatting, but make the replacement
match snprintf's bounded, explicitly terminated copy instead of assuming
the source byte after s_length is always its NUL. s_length is an int fed
from a size_t string length, so narrowing can produce a negative precision
or a smaller positive prefix. The ordinary short-query path remains a
small memcpy; the copied prefix is always bounded to the 128-byte buffer.

Copy at most buffer_size - 1 bytes and write the terminator explicitly.
This preserves the original negative-precision truncation behavior without
allocating multi-gigabyte input to exercise that edge during validation.
Long-input strdup selection and token splitting/ownership are unchanged.

Validation: optimized build passed; 31,694 ordinary differential tokenizer
cases still match the original implementation. Another 16 forced-length
cases exercise size_t-to-int narrowing, empty length and buffer boundaries,
checking copied bytes and termination against the original snprintf path.
No repository test files were modified. Benchmark results from 73f822839
remain labeled as that intermediate binary; this final bounded version
will receive its own matching unprofiled measurements.
---
 lib/c_tokenizer.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp b/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp
index 72c889c79..858315a6b 100644
--- a/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp
+++ b/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp
@@ -32,9 +32,12 @@ void tokenizer(tokenizer_t *result, const char* s, const char* delimiters, int e
 		if (result->s_length > (PROXYSQL_TOKENIZER_BUFFSIZE-1)) {
 			result->s = strdup(s);
 		} else {
-			// The length is already known and fits, including the terminator.
-			// Avoid invoking printf formatting for this per-query text copy.
-			memcpy(result->buffer, s, result->s_length + 1);
+			// Avoid printf formatting for this per-query text copy. Preserve its
+			// bound and explicit terminator even if s_length narrowed from size_t.
+			const size_t copy_length = (size_t)result->s_length < sizeof(result->buffer)
+				? (size_t)result->s_length : sizeof(result->buffer) - 1;
+			memcpy(result->buffer, s, copy_length);
+			result->buffer[copy_length] = '\0';
 			result->s = result->buffer;
 		}
 		}
